{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:16VernissageServer6MaxAgeO","modules":[{"name":"Vernissage"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaxAge","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MaxAge","symbolKind":"enum","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaxAge","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Enumeration"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaxAge","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"public","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" directive is included in a server’s HTTP response to indicate that it can be stored in a shared cache."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Caches are not permitted to store HTTP responses that contain the HTTP Authorization header unless they are accompanied by the public directive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"max-age","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directive is sent by a server to indicate that the HTTP response will remain fresh for a specified number of seconds after it is generated.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Essentially, it informs caches how long it will remain fresh. Importantly, the number of seconds indicates the period from which the content was generated,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as opposed to received. This means that any time spent in transit or stored in the caches of intermediaries is deducted from the allowance.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"immutable"},{"text":" directive indicates a guarantee by the server that the HTTP response will not be updated while it is still fresh.","type":"text"},{"tex